def max_fill(grid, capacity):
    import math
    return sum(math.ceil(sum(row) / capacity) for row in grid)
```

This function calculates the total number of times buckets need to be lowered to empty all the wells based on their capacities. It iterates over each row (well), sums up the units of water, divides by the bucket capacity and rounds up to get the number of trips needed for that well, then sums these values across all wells.

